A||||9||ChadMan||Buying from the Tire Rack||||5||
Z||000000||ChadMan||01-02-2001||03:09 PM||||Our New Year's Eve celebration was delayed by a cut sidewall on my wife's Saturn.  So I just ordered a pair of tires off the Tire Rack's Web site: <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tirerack.com</A>  .  Based on the quality of their site, their ads in Car and Driver and their reasonable prices, I'm optimistic that I'll be happy.  But it's always scary to do business by mail-order, especially off the Web.<P>Have any of you done business with the Tire Rack?  If so, were you happy?<P>They seem to have a lot of good tires around $50/each in the most common Fiero size (215/60R14).<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||01-02-2001||03:26 PM||||I bought my snow tires from them. They arrived on time and I didnt have any problums with them. I know a few other people that ordered tires from them and thought they were great.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||01-02-2001||03:28 PM||||What will be the cost of mounting and balancing, valve stem etc? Tire stores, even Wally world will do the mounting, balancing and valve stem replacement for the cost (slightly higher)of the tire.  Unless the tire is really inexpensive and you can do the install yourself, I don't know if you save that much.  The mounting is easy, the equipment to do it is expensive.<P>Do some comparative shopping against Pep Boys, Sam's Club and tire specialty store to see what the final cost is.||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||01-02-2001||04:34 PM||||i checked with a local service station, and they will charge $12/tire to mount.||||reg||2
Z||000004||ChadMan||01-02-2001||07:53 PM||||I have a buddy who manages a service station who will mount & balance tires for $10 apiece.  And I see no need to replace valve stems unless they're leaking.  So I should get away for around $130 including all surcharges.<P>Glad to hear of your positive experience, Master_Sushi.  Hope I have the same luck!||||reg||14
Z||000005||Black88GT||01-02-2001||09:07 PM||||My brother ordered his tires from them and they shipped pretty fast and the price was cheaper then the other 4 places he looked at.  His friend also got his tires from there and he was pleased with everything.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||14
Z||000006||PJ||01-02-2001||09:46 PM||||I've bought lots of tires and wheels (racing and street) from them over the past eight years. Good prices and fresh rubber (fresh means not laying around in hot storage for a year or two). They're also a major sponsor of the Sports Car Club of America. Next time call their 800 number. The sales reps are excellent. I love their cheap, fresh DOT race Kuhmos!||||reg||1
Z||000007||stomper282||01-02-2001||09:58 PM||||The tire rack is great for getting a good deal, but if you have any tire problems you have to go direct to the manufacture. That gets to be a pain in the rear.<BR> Thats just my 2 cents ||||reg||12
Z||000008||Greg Piet||01-03-2001||01:37 AM||||ewwww Kumho's    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>Hoosierdaddy!?!?!?!?!<P>but in all honesty kumho is better bang for the buck.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Slammed Fiero||01-03-2001||03:15 AM||||ordered my tr motorsports typhoons from then<BR>ordered a set of Kuhomo's for the porsche in september<BR>ordered a set of hoosiers for the corvair at the start of the summer... each came within 2 days of order, they followed up on the order to make sure we were happy. Great plce.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
